{
  "name": "ExplicitNullIsAPresentNullValue",
  "comment": "An explicit null is a real, typed, present value (Type \"null\") occupying the variable — it is\nNOT the same as a never-set variable (which resolves to not-found; WhereUnsetVariableIsNotFound\npins that side). Here we pin the value side: assigning null yields a present null-typed value\nthat reads back as null.",
  "step": [
